# sent_id = 1
# text = Der Motor wird vom Mechaniker repariert.
# lang = de
# note: "vom" is a multiword token. Stanza itself expands it correctly to the
# note: two words "von" (ADP, case) + "dem" (DET, det) -- the duplication below
# note: came from OUR round-trip, not from Stanza:
# note:   * MWT sub-words have start_char/end_char == None, so they inherit the
# note:     PARENT span (15:18);
# note:   * cas_conllu then re-derives FORM from get_covered_text() -> "vom"
# note:     twice, and looks up POS/LEMMA in dicts keyed by (begin,end), so the
# note:     two sub-words collide and one tag/lemma wins (hence the "varies
# note:     across runs" impression -- it is a dict collision, not randomness).
# note: HISTORICAL SHAPE ONLY. Both live parse paths now record each sub-word's
# note: true form as an MWTPart annotation -- preprocessing.stanza and (since
# note: the consistency fix) aslan_normalization._stanza_annotate -- and
# note: cas_conllu reads those back, so freshly parsed data yields von/dem as
# note: in positive_canonical_agent_de_mwt.conllu. This fixture is kept as the
# note: regression guard for data ingested BEFORE MWTPart existed, which still
# note: surfaces the contracted form, and is why the passive lexicon keeps
# note: "vom" in its agent-preposition set. It is a deliberate UD level-2
# note: exception (text-form-mismatch): the tokens cannot align to the text
# note: while both carry the surface form "vom".
